WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.938
Unit 5 covers policy and lifecycle.

2
00:00:02.938 --> 00:00:07.250
A policy assignment's enforcement mode
decides whether its effect applies.

3
00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:08.712
Default enforces it.

4
00:00:08.712 --> 00:00:13.523
Do not enforce still evaluates and
reports compliance, but prevents nothing:

5
00:00:13.523 --> 00:00:15.703
the right way to stage a deny policy,

6
00:00:15.703 --> 00:00:20.738
but one left there reports noncompliance
forever, so each needs a dated decision.

7
00:00:20.738 --> 00:00:24.038
Enroll enforces only
for enrolled resources.

8
00:00:24.038 --> 00:00:28.632
Running a version past its end of
support is NIST special publication

9
00:00:28.632 --> 00:00:33.463
eight hundred fifty-three's S A
twenty-two, unsupported system components.

10
00:00:33.463 --> 00:00:36.424
The dates come from
Microsoft's lifecycle pages.

11
00:00:36.424 --> 00:00:42.188
Windows Server 2012 is unsupported:
its extended security updates ended on

12
00:00:42.188 --> 00:00:47.950
October thirteenth, 2026, and Arc E S U
licenses were deactivated the next day.

13
00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:53.615
Windows Server 2016's extended support
ends January twelfth, 2027, and under the

14
00:00:53.615 --> 00:00:59.538
workbook's server standard, one still in
production after that date is an exception.

15
00:00:59.538 --> 00:01:07.588
SQL Server 2012 is unsupported, and
2014 and 2016 are in their E S U years.

16
00:01:07.588 --> 00:01:11.710
Where two Learn pages disagree,
the kit uses the earlier date.
